        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(e2e): bound OpenWebUI probe cleanup",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes (Codex)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the Open WebUI HTTP probe could return a successful response but then remain stuck while awaiting response body cancellation cleanup.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe probe still attempts to cancel the response body, but cleanup is now bounded by the probe's existing deadline signal so a never-settling body cancel cannot extend the probe indefinitely.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpen WebUI readiness checks keep their configured deadline even when response body cleanup does not settle.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `e39d33ba9d4971cf44b7622e457c3b4b06a28827`\n\n- Current-head package tarball build and integrity check passed with `node scripts/package-openclaw-for-docker.mjs --allow-unreleased-changelog --output-name openclaw-current.tgz`.\n- Open WebUI Docker smoke passed on the current-head package image with `OPENWEBUI_SMOKE_MODE=models OPENCLAW_OPENWEBUI_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.4-mini OPENCLAW_OPENWEBUI_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300 scripts/e2e/openwebui-docker.sh`: the Dockerized gateway started, Open WebUI signed in, `/api/models` returned through the gateway, resource checks passed (`memory=798.9MiB cpu=224.7% samples=23`), and the run finished with `OK`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/e2e-helper-env-limits.test.ts --reporter=verbose` passed: 11 tests.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Current-head checks `check-test-types`, `openclaw/ci-gate`, and `Real behavior proof` passed.",
